Z||000001||lennyb4||05-24-2000||11:36 AM||||Why would you want to fill them? Just curious? I roughed up the paint in mine(the one on the headlight cover), sanded it down, and filled it with silver paint then sealed it again with clear. Looks sweetttt..||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaveL||05-24-2000||04:01 PM||||Why, indeed, would anyone want to remove the "Pontiac" from a Pontiac? That would be like taking New York out of the city. Maybe rust problems.? I have noticed a few Fieros around lately that the owners have done some things with tail lights that make them appear to be shaped diferently, and one where the third brake light appears as the word "Poop" in red. I'm not sure thats quite legal, but it cracked me up when I got close enough to read it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||05-24-2000||08:39 PM||||I was thinking of and posted I may do so myself a while back after the way we have been recently treated at dealerships. Why advertise for them! I am a FIERO lover...I could give two sh*ts about PONTIAC!||||reg||8
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-24-2000||08:41 PM||||dont use epoxy, gets too hard/brittle itll crack back out. if u fill a hard panel use regular 2 part body filler. if its a 'soft' panel like a flexible bumper us 3M part #5895 (has 2 tubes-A & B). either way, you HAVE to remove all traces of paint and primer by sanding or wire brushing it out first. <P>rg||||reg||1
